# 17 Librarians and One Big Undertaking: Creating a Digital Project from Start to Finish

**Authors:** Hartsell-Gundy, Arianne, Lawton, Kelley, Rozear, Hannah

## Abstract
As academic librarians prepare for new forms of collaboration with researchers on digital projects, there is a growing demand for librarians to acquire skills with project management, as well as specific digital tools and methods. This article describes how research librarians collaborated together to complete a digital project related to student activism in the 1930s and 1940s on their campus. From researching in the archives to creating a digital timeline, the project utilized a team-based, &quot;learn by doing&quot; approach to allow librarians the opportunity to work through the logistics of a project from start to finish. The organization of the project, the digital tools and methods used, and the lessons learned are described in detail.

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ1246978

